d 'NTCOINT': module to provide test of nontrivial cointegration
d
d  ntcoint implements the squared-correlations ratio (SCR) test of
d Hualde, J. and J. Olmo (2026), "Testing for Nontrivial
d Cointegration", Journal of Business & Economic Statistics,
d doi:10.1080/07350015.2026.2638497. Standard cointegration methods
d cannot distinguish a genuine long-run equilibrium relationship
d from "trivial" cointegration, which arises merely because one of
d the series is stationary, so that a standard unit vector lies in
d the cointegrating space. Two independent processes, one I(0) and
d one I(1), are cointegrated in that formal sense while sharing no
d equilibrium at all. Testing for nontrivial cointegration with
d conventional tools requires a sequential procedure that is, in
d general, inconsistent. 
d
d KW: cointegration
d KW: stationarity
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261029
d
d Author:   Merwan Roudane, NA
d Support: email  merwanroudane920@@gmail.com
d
f ntcoint.ado
f ntcoint.sthlp
f ntcoint_authcv1.mata
f ntcoint_authcv2.mata
f ntcoint_cv1.mata
f ntcoint_cv2.mata
f ntcoint_ecbyields.do
f ntcoint_ecbyields.dta
f ntcoint_example.do
f ntcoint_methods.sthlp
